 "lines": [
  "Kai couldn't make a single sound.",
  "Saturday night. Thanksgiving leftovers. Kai laughed mid-bite.",
  "@am_echo: \"Kai? Dude, are you okay?\"",
  "Kai grabbed his throat with both hands. That's the universal sign for choking.",
  "If someone can cough hard, let them cough.",
  "But Kai couldn't cough, talk, or breathe. His airway was blocked.",
  "Choking kills thousands of Americans every year.",
  "@af_heart: \"Leo, call nine one one! I've got him!\"",
  "Without oxygen, brain damage can start in about four [minutes](minnits).",
  "Mia gave five hard back blows, right between the shoulder blades.",
  "Still stuck. His lips were starting to turn blue.",
  "Then five abdominal thrusts. A fist above the belly button, pulled hard, in and up.",
  "Each thrust forces air up out of the lungs, like a cork from a bottle.",
  "On the third thrust, the bite of turkey shot out.",
  "@am_michael: \"I can breathe. I can breathe!\"",
  "Still stuck? Keep switching, five and five. If they pass out, start CPR.",
  "@am_echo: \"But what if you're alone?\"",
  "Put a fist above your belly button, and thrust hard against a chair back.",
  "Here's the twist. Doctor [Heimlich](HYME-lick) introduced this move in nineteen seventy-four.",
  "In twenty sixteen, at ninety-six, he used it himself, on a woman choking at his senior home.",
  "She was eighty-seven, and it worked right away.",
  "So learn it. One day, someone next to you might go silent, like Kai."
 ],
